# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12 (Q45): a bare `return` in a block of a named Structure's body ends the
# execution there, as in a method's body -- n is 7, not 100 (before: "a Structure reference field needs a
# name").  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + 7U
    if: n = 7U
        return
    n: 100U
return
Counter
size_t: after 9U
after: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: after = 7U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
